# Plain `+` still TRAPS on overflow after `+%` and `+|` arrived: the new operators are
# how a program asks to wrap or clamp, never a change to what `+` means. A byte reaching
# 250 at run time plus 10 panics with Zig's message; the wrapping line before it prints 4.
# (`b` is assigned twice so it is a run-time value: a constant would be folded, and zig
# would refuse the overflow at build time instead of trapping.)
def main()
    var b: byte = 249
    b = b + 1
    print(b +% 10)
    print(b + 10)
    print("SURVIVED")
